# Line-ending policy
#
# This repo is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but its shell scripts EXECUTE ON LINUX
# (Yale Bouchet, SLURM). Under autocrlf=true git rewrites LF -> CRLF on checkout, and bash then
# reads the shebang/`set -euo pipefail` with a trailing \r:
#
#     submit_bbl_all.sh: line 51: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# (hit 2026-08-02 — every submit_* script failed at line 1 after upload). `eol=lf` pins these to
# LF in the working tree regardless of the local autocrlf setting, so what is uploaded always runs.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Julia/Python tolerate CRLF, so they are deliberately NOT forced here — normalizing them would
# rewrite most of the repo for no functional gain. Only add a pattern below when the file is
# consumed by something that breaks on \r.
